# The sum of two BallVectors with one-limb centers (milestone2.md, "BallVector": bv_add_k): the
# centers by add_1_1, entry by entry, as the map add_1; the state that of norm_upper_1 on the
# centers written, the largest magnitude and the mask that none was a NaN; the one radius
# bv_add_radius_1 at that magnitude, the largest of the radii of ball_add_1 entry by entry;
# norm_finish_1 tests that it is finite. When it is not (an operand is the whole space, or something
# overflowed), every center written is zero and the radius +infinity: the whole space.
fold:          bv_add_1
arrays:        stored x, stored y
scalars:       stored rx, stored ry
state:         m, mask ok
step:          z = add_1_1(x, y)
record:        (m, ok) = norm_step_1(m, ok, z)
combine:       (m, ok) = norm_combine(m, ok, m, ok)
radius:        rz = bv_add_radius_1(m, rx, ry)
finish:        (r, finite) = norm_finish_1(rz, ok)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z
output:        r
output:        mask finite
value:         x+y
requires:      ball_vector x rx
requires:      ball_vector y ry
ensures:       encloses_entries z r x+y x=x,rx y=y,ry flag=finite finite_when=abs_le(abs(x+y)+rx+ry,-2) radii_when=abs_le(rx+ry,-2) finite_from=2
min_precision: 1
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
source:        add_1_1 on the centers, the radius of ball_add_1 at the largest center (milestone2.md, BallVector)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
